Because \\(K\\) and \\(L\\) are points on the circles, and \\(AD\\) is parallel to \\(KL\\), the angles \\(\\angle ALC\\) and \\(\\angle ALC\\) are equal, implying that \\(\\angle O_1AN = \\angle O_2AN\\).\n\n4. **Conclusion:**\n   - The angle between the lines \\(O_1A\\) and \\(O_2N\\) is \\(90^\\circ\\). This is because \\(O_1A\\) is a radius of \\(\\omega_1\\) and \\(O_2A\\) is a radius of \\(\\omega_2\\), and the parallel lines \\(AD\\) and \\(KL\\) imply that the angle between the radii and the intersection point \\(N\\) is a right angle.\n\nThus, the angle between the lines \\(O_1A\\) and \\(O_2N\\) is \\(\\boxed{90^\\circ}\\)."}]
