[2026-04-07 08:01:56] [rlvr_pipeline.py (574)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 77670] [{"prompt": "system\nPlease reason step by step, and put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\nuser\nReturn your final response within \\boxed{}. Let $F \\subseteq E$ be a field extension. Suppose $\\alpha \\in E$ is a root of an irreducible polynomial $f(x)$ over $F$ with multiplicity $3$. If $\\beta$ is any other root of $f(x)$ in $E$, what is the multiplicity of $\\beta$?\nassistant\n", "response": "To determine the multiplicity of \\(\\beta\\), we start by analyzing the given information and the properties of polynomials over fields.\n\n1. **Given Information:**\n   - \\(F \\subseteq E\\) is a field extension.\n   - \\(\\alpha \\in E\\) is a root of an irreducible polynomial \\(f(x)\\) over \\(F\\) with multiplicity 3.\n   - \\(\\beta\\) is any other root of \\(f(x)\\) in \\(E\\).\n\n2. **Irreducibility and Roots:**\n   Since \\(f(x)\\) is irreducible over \\(F\\) and has \\(\\alpha\\) as a root with multiplicity 3, the polynomial \\(f(x)\\) can be written as:\n   \\[\n   f(x) = (x - \\alpha)^3 g(x)\n   \\]\n   where \\(g(x)\\) is a polynomial in \\(E[x]\\) that is coprime to \\(x - \\alpha\\) (i.e., \\(g(\\alpha) \\neq 0\\)).\n\n3. **Roots of \\(f(x)\\):**\n   Since \\(\\alpha\\) is a root of multiplicity 3, it is the only root of \\(x - \\alpha\\) in the factorization of \\(f(x)\\). The polynomial \\(g(x)\\) has no roots in \\(E\\) because it is coprime to \\(x - \\alpha\\).\n\n4. **Number of Roots:**\n   The polynomial \\(f(x)\\) is irreducible and has degree 3. Therefore, it has exactly 3 roots in its splitting field over \\(E\\), counting multiplicities. Since \\(\\alpha\\) is one of these roots with multiplicity 3, the other two roots must be \\(\\beta_1\\) and \\(\\beta_2\\), but \\(\\beta\\) is another root in \\(E\\).\n\n5. **Multiplicity of \\(\\beta\\):**\n   Since \\(\\beta\\) is a root of \\(f(x)\\) and \\(f(x)\\) is irreducible, \\(\\beta\\) must be a simple root of \\(f