}.\nuser\nReturn your final response within \\boxed{}. What is the sum of all positive integer divisors of 77?\nassistant\n", "response": "To find the sum of all positive integer divisors of 77, we start by determining its prime factorization. The number 77 can be factored as follows:\n\n\\[ 77 = 7 \\times 11 \\]\n\nSince 7 and 11 are both prime numbers, the prime factorization of 77 is \\(7^1 \\times 11^1\\).\n\nThe formula for the sum of the divisors of a number \\(n = p_1^{e_1} \\times p_2^{e_2} \\times \\cdots \\times p_k^{e_k}\\) is given by:\n\n\\[ \\sigma(n) = (1 + p_1 + p_1^2 + \\cdots + p_1^{e_1})(1 + p_2 + p_2^2 + \\cdots + p_2^{e_2}) \\cdots (1 + p_k + p_k^2 + \\cdots + p_k^{e_k}) \\]\n\nFor the number 77, which is \\(7^1 \\times 11^1\\), the sum of the divisors is:\n\n\\[ \\sigma(77) = (1 + 7)(1 + 11) \\]\n\nWe now calculate each term separately:\n\n\\[ 1 + 7 = 8 \\]\n\\[ 1 + 11 = 12 \\]\n\nMultiplying these together gives:\n\n\\[ \\sigma(77) = 8 \\times 12 = 96 \\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of all positive integer divisors of 77 is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{96} \\]"}, {"prompt": "system\nPlease reason step by step, and put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\nuser\nReturn your final response within \\boxed{}. What is the sum of all positive integer divisors of 77?\nassistant\n", "response": "To find the sum of all positive integer divisors of 77, we start by determining its prime factorization. The number 77 can be factored as follows:\n\\[ 77 = 7 \\times 11 \\]\nSince 7 and 11 are both prime numbers, the prime factorization of 77 is:\n\\[ 77 = 7^1 \\times 11^1 \\]\n\nThe formula for the sum of the divisors of a number \\( n = p_1^{e_1} \\times p_2^{e_2} \\times \\cdots \\times p_k^{e_k} \\) is:\n\\[ \\sigma(n) = (1 + p_1 + p_1^2 + \\cdots + p_1^{e_1})(1 + p_2 + p_2^2 + \\cdots + p_2^{e_2}) \\cdots (1 + p_k + p_k^2 + \\cdots + p_k^{e_k}) \\]\n\nFor the number 77, this becomes:\n\\[ \\sigma(77) = (1 + 7)(1 + 11) \\]\nWe calculate each term separately:\n\\[ 1 + 7 = 8 \\]\n\\[ 1 + 11 = 12 \\]\nSo, the sum of the divisors is:\n\\[ \\sigma(77) = 8 \\times 12 = 96 \\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of all positive integer divisors of 77 is:\n\\[ \\boxed{96} \\]"}]
