 the second part of the expression \\((x + 5)(2x - 1)\\):\n\n\\[\n(x + 5)(2x - 1) = x \\cdot 2x + x \\cdot (-1) + 5 \\cdot 2x + 5 \\cdot (-1) = 2x^2 - x + 10x - 5 = 2x^2 + 9x - 5\n\\]\n\nNow, we substitute these expanded forms back into the original expression:\n\n\\[\n(2x^2 + 9x - 35) - (2x^2 + 9x - 5)\n\\]\n\nWe distribute the negative sign through the second set of parentheses:\n\n\\[\n2x^2 + 9x - 35 - 2x^2 - 9x + 5\n\\]\n\nNext, we combine like terms:\n\n\\[\n(2x^2 - 2x^2) + (9x - 9x) + (-35 + 5) = 0 + 0 - 30 = -30\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the simplified form of the expression is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-30}\n\\]"}, {"prompt": "system\nPlease reason step by step, and put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\nuser\nReturn your final response within \\boxed{}. Simplify $(2x - 5)(x + 7) - (x + 5)(2x - 1)$.\nassistant\n", "response": "To simplify the expression \\((2x - 5)(x + 7) - (x + 5)(2x - 1)\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Expand each binomial product.\n2. Distribute the negative sign through the second expanded product.\n3. Combine like terms.\n\nLet's start with the first binomial product \\((2x - 5)(x + 7)\\):\n\n\\[\n(2x - 5)(x + 7) = 2x \\cdot x + 2x \\cdot 7 - 5 \\cdot x - 5 \\cdot 7 = 2x^2 + 14x - 5x - 35 = 2x^2 + 9x - 35\n\\]\n\nNext, expand the second binomial product \\((x + 5)(2x - 1)\\):\n\n\\[\n(x + 5)(2x - 1) = x \\cdot 2x + x \\cdot (-1) + 5 \\cdot 2x + 5 \\cdot (-1) = 2x^2 - x + 10x - 5 = 2x^2 + 9x - 5\n\\]\n\nNow, substitute these expanded forms back into the original expression and distribute the negative sign through the second expanded product:\n\n\\[\n(2x^2 + 9x - 35) - (2x^2 + 9x - 5) = 2x^2 + 9x - 35 - 2x^2 - 9x + 5\n\\]\n\nCombine like terms:\n\n\\[\n2x^2 - 2x^2 + 9x - 9x - 35 + 5 = 0 + 0 - 30 = -30\n\\]\n\nThus, the simplified form of the expression is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-30}\n\\]"}, {"prompt": "system\nPlease reason step by step, and put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\nuser\nReturn your final response within \\boxed{}. Simplify $(2x - 5)(x